 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **BVH Rebuild Cost:** The BVH must be rebuilt whenever the transfer function or iso-value changes, as the visibility of regions depends on the maximum opacity within their scalar ranges [S1]. On the Exajet dataset, a full rebuild takes approximately 300ms on a Titan RTX or RTX 8000 GPU [S1].
-*   **Transfer Function Changes:** Unlike methods that check region validity during traversal, this method excludes fully transparent regions from the BVH entirely [S1]. This avoids traversal checks but necessitates BVH updates for any transfer function change [S1].
-*   **Precision:** Using a new ray traversal for each iteration step means multiple hardware ray traversals per volume ray [S1]. Precision issues at region boundaries ($t_{out} + \epsilon$) must be handled to avoid gaps or overlaps [S1].
+*   **BVH Rebuild Cost:** The BVH must be rebuilt when the transfer function or iso-value changes. On the Exajet dataset, a full rebuild takes ~300ms on a Titan RTX or RTX 8000 [S1].
+*   **Transfer Function Changes:** Unlike methods that check region validity during traversal, this method requires a full BVH rebuild for any change in transfer function or iso-value, as regions are pruned based on precomputed opacity ranges [S1].
 
